## DESCRIPTION
## Find the length, dot product and angles between vectors.
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Euclidean spaces)
## DBsection(Vectors)
## Date(September 5, 2011)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## Level(1)
## KEYWORDS('length of vector', 'dot product', 'angle between vectors')

# updated 2022.12.12

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserVectorUtils.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Vector');

$u = ColumnVector(non_zero_vector3D(-5, 5));
$v = ColumnVector(non_zero_vector3D(-5, 5));
$w = ColumnVector([map { random(-5,5) } (0..3)]);
$x = ColumnVector([map { random(-5,5) } (0..3)]);


$Lu      = Real(norm($u));
$Lv      = Real(norm($v));
$DOTuv   = Compute("$u . $v");
$ANGLEuv = Compute("acos($DOTuv/($Lu*$Lv))");

$Lw      = Compute("sqrt($w . $w)");
$Lx      = Compute("sqrt($x . $x)");
$DOTwx   = Compute("$w . $x");
$ANGLEwx = Compute("acos($DOTwx/($Lw*$Lx))");

BEGIN_PGML

Consider the vectors [```
\vec{u} = [$u], \quad
\vec{v} = [$v], \quad
\vec{w} = [$w], \quad
\vec{x} = [$x].
```]


Find the following:

a) The length of [`\vec{u}`] is [___]{$Lu}

b) The dot product [`\vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} `]= [_____]{$DOTuv}

c) The angle between vectors [` \vec{u}`] and [` \vec{v}`] is [____]{$ANGLEuv}

d) The length of [` \vec{w} `] is [_____]{$Lw}

e) The angle between [`\vec{w} `] and [` \vec{x}`] is [_____]{$ANGLEwx}

Note: all angles should in radians.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Recall that the length of a vector [`\vec{u}`] or [`||\vec{u}||`] is
[```\vec{u} = \sqrt{u_1^2+u_2^2+ \cdots u_n^2}```].

The dot product beetween vectors [`\vec{u}`] and [`\vec{v}`] is
[```\vec{u}\cdot \vec{v} = u_1 v_1 + u_2 v_2 + \cdots + u_n v_n ```]

The angle between two vectors [`\vec{u}`] and [`\vec{v}`] can be found using
[```\cos(\theta) = \frac{\vec{u}\cdot\vec{v}}{||\vec{u}|| \; ||\vec{v}||}```]
a) [``||\vec{u}|| = \sqrt{[@ Compute("$u . $u") @]}``]

b) [`` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = [$DOTuv]``]

c) Angle between [`\vec{u}`] and [`\vec{v}`] is
[``\cos^{-1} \left(\frac{\vec{u} \cdot \vec{v}}{||\vec{u}|| \; ||\vec{v}||}\right)
= \cos^{-1} \frac{[$DOTuv]}{\sqrt{[@Compute("$u . $u")@]}\sqrt{[@Compute("$v.$v")@]}}
= [$ANGLEuv]``]

d) [``||\vec{x}|| = \sqrt{[@ Compute("$x . $x") @]}``]

e) Angle between [`\vec{w}`] and [`\vec{x}`] is
[``\cos^{-1} \left(\frac{\vec{w} \cdot \vec{x}}{||\vec{w}|| \; ||\vec{x}||}\right)
= \cos^{-1} \frac{[$DOTwx]}{\sqrt{[@Compute("$w.$w")@]}\sqrt{[@Compute("$x.$x")@]}}
= [$ANGLEwx]``]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
